C1. Concepts of Decision Support System (DSS)

A Decision Support System (DSS) is a computer based system that helps users to make decisions by collecting, processing and analyzing important information. 
It supports the decision making process by evaluate different alternatives and provide useful information to help users select a suitable option.

According to Kovari (2024), Ai based DSS can analyze large amounts of information and provide recommendations to support the decision making. 
However, the accuracy, transparency and liability of recommendations are important to maintain user trust.

In purposed of MyRapid KL Intelligent Decision Support System (DSS) is to help public transportation users make a better travel decision. 
For example, when train service is disrupted, the system can discover available transportation information and generates alternative route recommendations.
Users then can compare before choosing their preference route


KEY CONCEPTS OF DECISION SUPPORT SYSTEM (DSS)

1.	Data Driven Decision Making:
Data driven decision making refers to use of relevant information to support a decision making process. 
DSS will collect and study available data to provide useful information for the users. In the proposed for MyRapid KL Pulse system,
information of transportation such as train service disruption, alternative routes, estimated travel time and crowd level is used to support route recommendations.

2.	Interactive Decision Supports:
Interactive decision support allow users to communicate with the system by interring information and view the results or recommendation will provide. 
In the proposed for this system, users can enter their starting location and their destination through a search bar. The system then will display relevant 
route information and alternative recommendation routes.

3.	Human Decision Making:
DSS is designed to support human decision by providing useful information and recommendations. However, users can still make their final decision based on 
their needs and preference. In this system, users can see the recommended routes and choose whether to accept or decline the suggestion route. 
